            "text_mQ6HX7": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Long before our current home on Campbell Street, Storm put up shop in what is now Tofino's laundromat. It was 1997, and Tofino was still a well-kept secret, less the few dedicated PNW surfers, whispering about a wave north island.</p><p>What started as a place to get your gear sorted became something more: a gathering point for anyone who felt the pull of the Pacific. Friends, locals, travellers passing through. </p>",
